---
/*
  PageHeader — the top of every admin page: an optional back link, the title
  (or a `title` slot when the title is an editable field), a right-aligned
  actions cluster, and an optional one-line explanation. Keeps the workshop's
  surfaces from each inventing their own header geometry.

  ⚠ THE ACTIONS SLOT IS WHERE A ROOM'S CREATE DOOR GOES, and what that door is
  CALLED had no rule until 2026-08-17 (plan 42 · §4.C.10). The tree said: New
  (tasks, goals) · New constellation · New event · Add (people) · Add ▾
  (fragments) · Add (placement) · ＋ (shared-by) — and it did not split on any
  line anyone could name, since People and Tasks are both HQ and disagree.

  THE RULE, derived from what the tree already does rather than invented:
  **the door names the noun only when the page around it does not.**

    Tasks      h1 "Tasks"           → New                    ✓
    Goals      h1 "Goals"           → New                    ✓
    People     h1 "People"          → Add                    ✓
    Calendar   no h1 naming events  → New event              ✓
    Fragments  makes TWO kinds      → Add ▾ (nouns on items) ✓
    Constellations  h1 "Constellations" → New constellation  ✗

  ⚠ FIVE OF SIX ALREADY KEEP IT AND THE SIXTH IS REDUNDANT WITH ITS OWN HEADING.
  `/admin/constellations` says the word twice, 40px apart. It is not worth a
  commit of its own — fold it to "New" whenever that file is next open. Recorded
  rather than fixed, so the exception reads as known instead of as the precedent.

  ⚠ AND ON *Add* VERSUS *New*: Add where the thing joins something that already
  exists — a roster, a suite, a shelf (a person, a placement, a shared-by link).
  New where the room brings it into being (a task, a goal, an event). The
  fragment manager's **Add ▾** is the one that breaks this and earns it: its
  trigger only has to say *there is a menu here*, and the nouns are on the items.

  ⚠ CONSEQUENCE FOR A ROOM THAT DOES NOT EXIST YET (plan 42 · §4.D.2): the sets
  sheet's door is **"New"**, not "New set" — `/admin/sets` already carries an h1
  reading Sets. The plan said "New set" before this rule was written down, which
  is exactly the coin-flip a stated rule removes.
*/
import BackLink from './BackLink.astro';

interface Props {
  title?: string;
  /** A single level up — the workshop is never deeper than that. */
  back?: { href: string; label: string };
  subtitle?: string;
  class?: string;
}
const { title, back, subtitle, class: className = '' } = Astro.props;
---

<header class:list={['mb-6', className]}>
  {/* The same component the two custom-header pages use — see BackLink. */}
  {back && <BackLink href={back.href} label={back.label} class="mb-2" />}
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
    <div class="min-w-0 grow">
      {title ? <h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-light">{title}</h1> : <slot name="title" />}
    </div>
    <div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-2">
      <slot name="actions" />
    </div>
  </div>
  {subtitle && <p class="text-base-content/55 mt-2 max-w-2xl font-sans text-sm">{subtitle}</p>}
</header>
